{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Swami","externalID":"Swami","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state graph (computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":") rather than imperative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragrap